WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:05.320
NGF keeps neurons alive.

2
00:00:06.200 --> 00:00:08.080
Does it also choose where their axons go?

3
00:00:09.050 --> 00:00:12.690
A permissive signal allows an outcome that something else chooses.

4
00:00:13.550 --> 00:00:16.150
An instructive signal chooses the outcome itself.

5
00:00:17.233 --> 00:00:18.913
Fuel lets a car go anywhere.

6
00:00:19.873 --> 00:00:20.873
The driver picks where.

7
00:00:21.693 --> 00:00:22.693
Fuel is permissive.

8
00:00:23.513 --> 00:00:25.013
The driver is instructive.

9
00:00:25.867 --> 00:00:30.607
Removing a signal and restoring its normal pattern cannot tell the two apart.

10
00:00:31.447 --> 00:00:33.067
It only shows the signal is needed.

11
00:00:34.100 --> 00:00:38.220
Instead, keep the signal present, but change where or when it is delivered.

12
00:00:39.200 --> 00:00:40.980
Then ask whether the pattern still forms.

13
00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:46.440
If the pattern stays put, something else reads position, and the signal was

14
00:00:46.440 --> 00:00:50.660
permissive. If the pattern follows the delivery, it is instructive.

15
00:00:51.550 --> 00:00:57.950
In 1989, Edwards and colleagues directed NGF to the pancreatic islets of otherwise

16
00:00:57.950 --> 00:00:58.950
normal mice.

17
00:00:59.750 --> 00:01:04.370
Islets are small clusters of hormone-making cells scattered through the pancreas.

18
00:01:05.283 --> 00:01:08.623
Predict. Where do the sympathetic fibres go?

19
00:01:14.567 --> 00:01:16.687
Innervation of the islets rose sharply.

20
00:01:17.547 --> 00:01:19.667
The surrounding tissue gained no matching rise.

21
00:01:20.567 --> 00:01:21.887
The pattern followed the delivery.

22
00:01:25.917 --> 00:01:29.517
In 1993, Hoyle and colleagues ran the converse test.

23
00:01:30.477 --> 00:01:33.977
Their mice had sympathetic neurons that made NGF themselves.

24
00:01:35.117 --> 00:01:39.217
Now NGF was made by the neurons too, not only by the target.

25
00:01:40.267 --> 00:01:42.067
Axons still reached their tissues.

26
00:01:42.987 --> 00:01:44.967
But inside them, they branched sparsely.

27
00:01:45.900 --> 00:01:50.240
Making NGF in the islets of these mice restored islet innervation.

28
00:01:51.350 --> 00:01:56.410
So, in the sympathetic targets tested, NGF is permissive for reaching a target.

29
00:01:57.433 --> 00:02:01.993
It is instructive for how densely, and where, axons innervate within it.

30
00:02:02.673 --> 00:02:04.133
Here the fuel analogy breaks.

31
00:02:05.133 --> 00:02:11.293
One more test. In mice lacking both NGF and Bax, sympathetic neurons survive.

32
00:02:12.367 --> 00:02:15.567
With death blocked, any defect left is not about survival.

33
00:02:16.567 --> 00:02:18.507
They fail to innervate many of their targets.

34
00:02:19.567 --> 00:02:20.847
Put the lesson together.

35
00:02:21.767 --> 00:02:22.847
The target is needed.

36
00:02:23.807 --> 00:02:25.347
Adding NGF saves neurons.

37
00:02:26.327 --> 00:02:29.027
Removing it, by antibody or by gene, kills them.

38
00:02:29.967 --> 00:02:33.307
The TrkA mutant shows the neurons were made, then lost.

39
00:02:34.447 --> 00:02:39.187
Acting as a survival factor, NGF cannot raise survivors above the number made.

40
00:02:40.200 --> 00:02:44.920
NGF keeps already specified neurons alive, and types differ in that need.

41
00:02:45.820 --> 00:02:48.640
Where it is supplied helps decide which connections stay.

42
00:02:49.633 --> 00:02:54.133
How some neurons come to win is the subject of the lesson on competition for

43
00:02:54.133 --> 00:02:55.133
targets.

44
00:02:55.567 --> 00:02:58.627
Takeaway: for survival, NGF is permissive.

45
00:02:59.487 --> 00:03:02.367
Within a target, it also instructs where axons branch.
